From 715de0e2d21bb2cd3e60307f0b572486d7397980 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Catalin Niculescu <cn.cata@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:59:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] llano.py off: the pad off; speed 0 keeps it on, lights too

Stopping the fan takes on_off, which puts the lights out with it, and the
pad has no fan-off-lights-on. So `off` is its own command (the whole pad
off, fan and lights), and `speed 0` is the pad on at 0 %: lights on, the
fan at its slowest, 300 rpm on the pad's display (like 1 %). `lock` uses
off and records whether the pad was off, so `unlock` restores that too.
noise.py: 0 % is 300 rpm; a pad switched off is 0 rpm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 NOISE.md  |  2 +-
 README.md |  7 ++++---
 llano.py  | 27 ++++++++++++++++++---------
 noise.py  | 12 +++++++-----
 4 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

